<Project DefaultTargets="Build" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/developer/msbuild/2003">

  <!--
    iOS links native code into the application rather than loading it, so an archive sitting
    under runtimes/ios-arm64/native/ is inert weight until something tells the build to link
    it. That is what this file does; without it the package would carry archives no consumer
    could ever use, which is the state KTX.NET is in today.

    The settings are taken from Evergine.Bindings.JoltPhysics, which measured them against a
    real link. They are reproduced rather than reinvented:

    _FrameworkNativeReference, injected before _ComputeLinkNativeExecutableInputs, is the shape
    that went green there. A public NativeReference item may well work too; that was never
    validated, and this file is not the place to find out.

    ForceLoad, because the linker takes only the archive members something references, and every
    entry point here is reached from managed code. Without it the application builds and defines
    none of the tvg_ symbols.

    SmartLink, because iOS links with -dead_strip: ForceLoad pulls every member in and the strip
    takes back out whatever nothing references. SmartLink has the SDK read the assembly's
    P/Invokes and pass -u for each, naming them as roots the strip must keep.

    Which runtime identifier to use is decided by $(RuntimeIdentifier), because an iOS build may
    target a device or the simulator and those are separate architectures — there is no fat
    archive here.

    NOT VERIFIED: no iOS application has been linked against this package. ThorVG bundles its
    own png/jpg/webp decoders under -Dstatic=true, so if a consuming application also links
    libpng, libjpeg or libwebp, -force_load can surface duplicate symbols. That is the one place
    this precedent may fail to carry over, and it would appear as a link error rather than
    anything subtle.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'ios'">
    <_ThorVGIosRid Condition="'$(_ThorVGIosRid)' == ''">$(RuntimeIdentifier)</_ThorVGIosRid>
    <_ThorVGIosRid Condition="'$(_ThorVGIosRid)' == ''">ios-arm64</_ThorVGIosRid>
    <_ThorVGIosArchive>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../runtimes/$(_ThorVGIosRid)/native/libthorvg.a</_ThorVGIosArchive>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <Target Name="EvergineThorVGAddIosNativeReference"
          BeforeTargets="_ComputeLinkNativeExecutableInputs"
          Condition="$([MSBuild]::GetTargetPlatformIdentifier('$(TargetFramework)')) == 'ios' And Exists('$(_ThorVGIosArchive)')">
    <ItemGroup>
      <_FrameworkNativeReference Include="$(_ThorVGIosArchive)">
        <Kind>Static</Kind>
        <ForceLoad>true</ForceLoad>
        <SmartLink>true</SmartLink>
      </_FrameworkNativeReference>
    </ItemGroup>
  </Target>

</Project>
